  "provisional": "A PC's memory fixes how much the NPU can hold (about half of it), which gives three sizes: Flash, Flux and Forge. Each size is a pack of models of that size, each the best at one kind of work. Every repo and its Q4_0 file was checked on Hugging Face (October 2026). The choice of model for each kind of work rests on the independent scores that exist (the Vectara hallucination leaderboard, checked on its page, for facts and summaries; BigCodeBench-Hard, from a report, for code) and otherwise on judgement, which each line says. Speeds marked est. are estimates (about 37 GB/s of memory bandwidth ÷ file size) and are replaced by what your PC measures. The 2B, 4B and 9B packs were then re-chosen from the app's own benchmark (30 models run on a Snapdragon X NPU, 33 tests each, one to four tests per kind of work): a model replaces another only where it is clearly better, and the 14B and 24B packs are unchanged because the benchmark PC could not load anything bigger than 9B.",
